TECH TIERS:
	Terratech comes in tech tiers, which is how involved the player needs to be in order to get ahold if it.
	While the tech tiers doesn't matter much at the moment, it very much will later on.
	The higher the tech tiers, the stronger the tech is - and the more reactive an Ecotech faction will be when an Industrial faction gets ahold of it.

	-1: COMMONPLACE: Anyone can get ahold of this, with little to no research. this goes up to Periwood Basics.
	-2: SENSITIVE: This is where factions start guarding their tech, and players need to show dedication. The following is required:
		-The player gets a debuff for having industrial+ structures on the map.
		-Conduit Trees function slower if industrial+ structures are on the map (except Reclaimer tree)
		-Terratech structures will start to wither away with too many industrial+ structures.
		-Factions may ask for Terratech back if on good or bad terms, but may also be lenient.
		-This starts at Elderwood applications (T2), and goes up to T3 tech.
	-3: DEVOTED: Only those who have proven they are fully committed to Terratech can have Devoted tech.
		-Devoted Tech and higher is explicity outlawed to anyone Industrial+. The tech being returned will be demanded, or seizure squads may be sent in.
		-If a Neolithic-Medieval faction has this tech, lenience may be shown if they are on goodwill AND the faction agrees to embrace Terratech. Otherwise, the tech must be returned.
		-Some devoted tech requires meditations.
	-4: CRUX: The pinnacle and most applicable of Terratech. Only those that have fully embraced all Terratech havbe access to this tier.
		-Gaining access to Crux Terratech as an Industrial+ faction results in a permanent -100 reputation with Ecotech factions.
		-Additionally, they'll launch yearly purging raids; raids that include all three factions.
		-Most Crux tech lines requires meditation to discover. This can be done faster if done cooperatively.
		-The player gains a +100 bonues with one Ecotech faction, and +50 with the other two.
	-5: OBSCURED: Tech that doesn't fall into any category, and is likely just arcotech.
		-Seen as gifts or sacred relics. Generally follows the rules of Crux.
		-Certain items from these techs can be aquired from quests, or other special methods.
		-One rare item may also allow an Industrial colony to freely use Ecotech without worry.

